0..48 Comment "//! A freshness condition limits a nominal rule."
49..52 Comment "//!"
53..131 Comment "//! A `where a # q` clause states that atom `a` is outside the support of `q`."
132..135 Comment "//!"
136..208 Comment "//! A rule that moves a variable across an abstraction needs a freshness"
209..285 Comment "//! condition. The description check refuses capture without that condition."
286..362 Comment "//! Each `Theory` value stores a condition as a `Fresh` link after its rule."
363..432 Comment "//! These theories have no atom ports. Their term supports are empty."
433..436 Comment "//!"
437..484 Comment "//! - cites: [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]"
485..555 Comment "//! - cites: [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]"
556..559 Comment "//!"
560..683 Comment "//! [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2006.12.002 \"Fernández and Gabbay, Nominal rewriting\""
684..849 Comment "//! [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]: https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139084673 \"Pitts, Nominal Sets: Names and Symmetry in Computer Science\""
